Create nested morphism images during closure

Nested morphism definitions must allocate a result when a conclusion
requires an image that does not yet exist. Recover a valid mapped parent
chain using the same membership checks as insertion, then create the
result in that chain instead of requiring closure to have created it.

Reproduce the closure panic with an evaluation regression test. Cover
deeper images, preserved outer parents, shared source membership, and
noncanonical arguments so creation respects dependent types.
